From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 20:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: describe the fuel gauge

The handset has a TI BQ27541 fuel gauge, which the driver already supports
under the ti,bq27541 compatible. Nothing described it, so the only battery
information available came from the charger, leaving charge level, capacity,
current and temperature unreported.

The stock device tree places it at address 0x55 on the eighth QUP serial
engine, alongside the fast-charge microcontroller. That engine is i2c8 here
and was not enabled.

monitored-battery is deliberately omitted. The gauge is factory programmed
for the cell it ships with, and on chips with writable data memory the
driver can push devicetree values into it, which is not something a
description should do to a working battery.

Signed-off-by: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -363,6 +363,16 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&i2c8 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	fuel-gauge@55 {
+		compatible = "ti,bq27541";
+		reg = <0x55>;
+	};
+};
+
 &i2c17 {
 	status = "okay";
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
--
2.50.1
